---@class vercel.marketplace.GetInvoiceResponse
---@field created string System creation date. ISO 8601 timestamp.
---@field discounts? vercel.marketplace.GetInvoiceResponseDiscountsList Invoice discounts.
---@field externalId? string Partner-supplied Invoice ID, if applicable.
---@field invoiceDate string Invoice date. ISO 8601 timestamp.
---@field invoiceId string Vercel Marketplace Invoice ID.
---@field invoiceNumber? string User-readable invoice number.
---@field items vercel.marketplace.GetInvoiceResponseItemsList Invoice items.
---@field memo? string Additional memo for the invoice.
---@field outstandingTotal? string Amount still owed on the invoice, per the payment processor. Can be positive even for states "refunded" or "refund_requested", since a refund does not settle an unpaid remainder. A dollar-based decimal string. Absent when no payment data is available yet.
---@field paidAt? string Moment the invoice was paid. ISO 8601 timestamp.
---@field paidTotal? string Total amount paid and retained: payments received minus refunds applied. A dollar-based decimal string. Absent when no payment data is available yet.
---@field pendingRefundTotal? string Requested refund amount not yet applied by the payment processor: "refundTotal" minus "refundedTotal". A dollar-based decimal string. Only present when a refund was requested or applied.
---@field period vercel.marketplace.GetInvoiceResponsePeriod Subscription period for this billing cycle. ISO 8601 timestamps.
---@field refundedAt? string Most recent moment the invoice was refunded. ISO 8601 timestamp.
---@field refundedTotal? string Total refund amount applied by the payment processor, on the same pre-tax basis as "refundTotal". Counts both money returned and debt cancelled on unpaid invoices. May be lower than "refundTotal", which is the requested amount. A dollar-based decimal string. Only present when a refund was requested or applied.
---@field refundReason? string The reason for refund. Only present when a refund has been requested.
---@field refundTotal? string Total refund amount requested. Only present when a refund has been requested. A dollar-based decimal string.
---@field state vercel.marketplace.GetInvoiceResponseState Invoice state. Reports the payment state of the invoice; refund progress is reported separately via "refundedTotal" and "pendingRefundTotal". The states "refunded" and "refund_requested" only appear when the payment state cannot be determined.
---@field test? boolean Whether the invoice is in the testmode (no real transaction created).
---@field total string Invoice total amount. A dollar-based decimal string.
---@field updated string System update date. ISO 8601 timestamp.

